<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-bs-theme="dark">

<head>
  <%- include('partials/head', {
    title: 'FAQs - Countic',
    description: 'How Countic updates counters, languages, categories and troubleshooting for YouTube, Twitch and Kick panels.',
    canonicalPath: '/faqs',
  }); %>
</head>

<body id="top" class="d-flex flex-column min-vh-100">

  <%- include('partials/header', { active: 'faqs' }); %>

  <main class="container my-5">
    <%
      const supportLink = '<a href="https://discord.gg/kKRnpfR" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-decoration-none fw-bold text-primary-emphasis border-bottom">Support Server</a>';
    %>
    <h1 class="text-center mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
    <p class="lead text-center">Answers to the most common questions about Countic. Anything missing? Ask in the
      <%- supportLink %>.</p>

    <%
      const faqItems = [
        {
          question: 'How often do counters update?',
          answer: `YouTube counters refresh every hour, Twitch and Kick counters every 15 minutes. Updates run on a fixed
            schedule, nobody has to type anything to trigger them.`,
        },
        {
          question: 'Does the bot read our messages?',
          answer: `No. Countic has no access to messages, its Discord intents do not include them. Updates are
            driven by a timer, not by activity.`,
        },
        {
          question: 'Why is YouTube slower than Twitch and Kick?',
          answer: `YouTube limits its API with a daily quota. Countic batches many channels into a single request to use as
            little quota as possible, which makes one update per hour per panel sustainable for thousands of servers.
            Twitch and Kick APIs have no such quota, so they update every 15 minutes.`,
        },
        {
          question: 'How do I rename the category?',
          answer: `Run <code>/customize template</code> and pick the category counter, then write any plain text, for
            example <code>[name] • My Community</code> or just <code>My Community</code>. <code>[name]</code> is optional
            and inserts the tracked channel's name, so a template without it keeps a fixed label that no longer follows
            channel renames. Stat placeholders like <code>[subs]</code> are not allowed in the category.`,
        },
        {
          question: 'Can I change the language?',
          answer: `There is nothing to configure. Replies follow each member's own Discord client language, currently English
            and Turkish. Counter numbers follow the server language setting, so a Turkish server gets
            <code>1,23M</code> while an English server gets <code>1.23M</code>.`,
        },
        {
          question: 'Can I track multiple channels?',
          answer: `One panel per platform per server, which means a YouTube, a Twitch and a Kick panel can run side by side,
            each following its own channel.`,
        },
        {
          question: 'A counter stopped updating, what now?',
          answer: `Run <code>/panel status</code>. Every counter is listed with its state and the reason if it stopped, for
            example missing permissions or a deleted channel. Fix the cause and run <code>/setup</code> again to recreate
            the panel, your counter templates are kept.`,
        },
        {
          question: 'How do I remove Countic from my server?',
          answer: `Run <code>/panel delete</code>, which removes the category, its counter channels and the stored settings.
            If you remove the bot without deleting the panel first, the counters stay as ordinary voice channels you can
            delete by hand. Stored settings are purged automatically within 7 days.`,
        },
      ];
    %>
    <div class="accordion col-lg-8 mx-auto" id="faqAccordion">
      <% faqItems.forEach((item, index) => {
        const open = index === 0;
        const id = `collapse${index + 1}`;
        const headingId = `heading${index + 1}`;
      %>
      <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header" id="<%= headingId %>">
          <button class="accordion-button<%= open ? '' : ' collapsed' %>" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#<%= id %>" aria-expanded="<%= open %>" aria-controls="<%= id %>">
            <%= item.question %>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="<%= id %>" class="accordion-collapse collapse<%= open ? ' show' : '' %>" aria-labelledby="<%= headingId %>" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
          <div class="accordion-body">
            <%- item.answer %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <% }); %>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-4 text-center">
      Still have questions? Join the <%- supportLink %> and ask.
    </p>
  </main>

  <%- include('partials/footer'); %>
</body>

</html>
